From: opencode-android <opencode-android@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] tui: gate thinking-block expand on completion

Tapping the streaming "Thinking" header (ReasoningPart, hide mode)
calls toggle -> setExpanded while reasoning deltas are still arriving,
which mounts the <code streaming> block mid-stream and aborts the
native renderer on Android (SIGABRT in the TUI, no JS error logged).
Tapping the completed "Thought" header mounts it with final content
and is safe.

Guard two ways:
  * toggle() no-ops until the part is finalized (isDone)
  * the onMouseUp handler is only attached once done, so no JS
    mouse callback runs while the spinner is live

Taps on a still-streaming thinking block become a no-op; expand
works as soon as the block turns into "Thought".
---
 packages/tui/src/routes/session/message-parts.tsx | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/tui/src/routes/session/message-parts.tsx b/packages/tui/src/routes/session/message-parts.tsx
--- a/packages/tui/src/routes/session/message-parts.tsx
+++ b/packages/tui/src/routes/session/message-parts.tsx
@@ -66,4 +66,7 @@ export function ReasoningPart(props: {
   const toggle = () => {
-    if (!inMinimal()) return
+    // Expanding while reasoning still streams mounts the <code> block
+    // mid-stream and aborts the native renderer on Android (tap SIGABRT).
+    // Keep taps during streaming a no-op; expand once the part is done.
+    if (!inMinimal() || !isDone()) return
     setExpanded((prev) => !prev)
   }
@@ -78,5 +81,5 @@ export function ReasoningPart(props: {
           paddingLeft={!inMinimal() || expanded() ? 1 : 0}
         >
-          <box onMouseUp={toggle}>
+          <box onMouseUp={isDone() ? toggle : undefined}>
             <ReasoningHeader
               toggleable={inMinimal()}
